  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="ff48513c-97c3-5930-8da1-829ad4b91d59" activityNameId="6750bee0-258d-5e55-bf49-0d3bf757e6c3" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Transport, freight helicopter, single-engine, Betrieb</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Transport, freight helicopter, single-engine, Betrieb
A single engine helicopter of the type ecureuil-as-350-b3  with a weight of 1200kg and a life time of 10000 flight hours is assumed. The average flight duration is assumed to be 20min and 3 LTO per hour is required. Specific cruise emission factors for a ecureuil-as-350-b3 helicopter is provided of the federal office of civil aviation (FOCCA);
UUID: 62060214-4151-3278-b116-1dc7f7812ef5
This dataset describes the demand of helicopter, demand of LTOs, energy requirements and emissions of one hour helicopter flight.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Data is for an average Swiss helicopter for observation flights (1280kg) using kerosene
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: 13500h
Sampling: Statistics 
Extrapolations: helicopter input is extrapolated by a medium haul aircraft.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_62060214-4151-3278-b116-1dc7f7812ef5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
